LOK Calc: a new chart lands beside its data

FuInsertChart placed a chart away from aPositionRange, which for
request arguments (a kit client gives the range in FN_PARAM_5) was the
cursor cell alone; GetChartInsertPos then pulled the chart back into
the visible area. The chart covered the data it charts, or a block
next to it. Under LOK, with a requested range, the chart goes in the
first empty, unmerged cells of its own sheet right of its data large
enough for it, else below, left or above, else the first such block
anywhere, whatever the visible area. Data on another sheet starts the
search at the cursor. With no room on the sheet the insert fails and
nothing lands. Sizes are summed from each candidate cell.

